(V_j) = \\bigcup U_{ji}$\nsuch that $\\mathcal{O}_Y(V) \\to \\mathcal{O}_X(U)$ is a formally smooth\nring map for all $j$ and $i$."], "proof_screened": false, "provisional_durable_scope_assertions": [], "schema": "maththm.section-walk-candidate.v1", "section_label": "section-formally-smooth", "section_opening_preview": null, "section_start_line": 3051, "section_title": "Formally smooth morphisms", "source_filename": "more-morphisms.tex", "source_label": "lemma-formally-smooth", "source_revision": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_statement_line": 3332, "source_url": "https://github.com/stacks/stacks-project/blob/a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14/more-morphisms.tex#L3332", "statement_tex": "\\label{lemma-formally-smooth}\nLet $f : X \\to Y$ be a morphism of schemes. The following are equivalent:\n\\begin{enumerate}\n\\item $f$ is formally smooth,\n\\item for every $x \\in X$ there exist opens $x \\in U \\subset X$ and\n$f(x) \\in V \\subset Y$ with $f(U) \\subset V$ such that\n$f|_U : U \\to V$ is formally smooth,\n\\item for every pair of affine opens $U \\subset X$ and $V \\subset Y$\nwith $f(U) \\subset V$ the ring map $\\mathcal{O}_Y(V) \\to \\mathcal{O}_X(U)$\nis formally smooth, and\n\\item there exists an affine open covering $Y = \\bigcup V_j$ and\nfor each $j$ an affine open covering $f^{-1}(V_j) = \\bigcup U_{ji}$\nsuch that $\\mathcal{O}_Y(V) \\to \\mathcal{O}_X(U)$ is a formally smooth\nring map for all $j$ and $i$.\n\\end{enumerate}", "statement_truncated": false}
